DESCRIPTION

  A lua-zlib compatible binding over the zlib already vendored in
  third_party/zlib.  Hand-written, not vendored.

  lua-http's http/zlib.lua accepts either of the two Lua bindings that
  claim the module name "zlib", picking its calling convention from the
  _VERSION string.  This presents the lua-zlib one, because that
  interface is a pair of stream closures and maps cleanly onto zlib's
  own inflate and deflate.

  Only what http/zlib.lua uses is implemented: _VERSION, inflate() and
  deflate().

LOCAL DEVIATION

  lua-zlib defaults deflate's windowBits to MAX_WBITS, which is the raw
  zlib framing.  This defaults to MAX_WBITS+16, which is gzip, because
  the only caller is lua-http and the only thing it does with the output
  is serve it as `transfer-encoding: gzip`.  Pass windowBits explicitly
  for other framings.  inflate defaults to automatic detection of either,
  which matches lua-zlib.
